Description: TrueNAS cross-BE upgrade helper scripts
 Stdlib-only scripts that run across boot-environment (BE) boundaries
 during TrueNAS install and upgrade:
 .
   * truenas-initrd.py reconciles boot-environment configuration files
     with the TrueNAS configuration database and regenerates the initramfs
     for each kernel installed in the target BE.
   * truenas-grub.py lays down /etc/default/grub.d/truenas.cfg in the
     target BE from a pre-rendered snapshot at
     /data/subsystems/grub/truenas.cfg that middlewared maintains on the
     live system.
 .
 The scripts and the sibling `upgrade_pyutils` helper package ship
 together. The package deliberately depends on nothing outside the
 Python standard library because these scripts are invoked across
 boot-environment boundaries during install and upgrade, where loading
 third-party code from the host BE's site-packages would risk Python
 ABI / kernel-feature mismatches.
